Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:07:11 +0200
Subject: [M155] [objects] Prevent map normalization of remote objects

Original change's description:
> [objects] Prevent map normalization of remote objects
>
> When `Object.assign` encounters a source object with a large number of
> properties, `JSReceiver::SetOrCopyDataProperties` pre-normalizes the
> target object to a dictionary map.
>
> If the target object is a remote object (a JS_SPECIAL_API_OBJECT_TYPE
> whose map is contextless), it possesses no `NativeContext`.
> `Map::Normalize` was previously unconditionally casting the `Null` native
> context of the remote object's meta-map to a `NativeContext`, leading
> to an out-of-bounds ReadOnly memory access and eventually OOB writes.
>
> This patch updates `JSReceiver::SetOrCopyDataProperties` to exclude
> contextless `JS_SPECIAL_API_OBJECT_TYPE` targets from normalization,
> properly handling them alongside global proxies and shared structs,
> which natively lack a context. It also replaces the potential silent
> crash in `Map::Normalize` with a `DCHECK`.
>
> Fixed: 562038980
>
