Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
Chromium 148's V8 predates the InstanceTypeChecker-based rewrite of the
SetOrCopyDataProperties() condition (it still uses IsJSObject(*target) /
!IsJSGlobalProxy(*target) and has no IsAlwaysSharedSpaceJSObject check),
so the remote-object exclusion is added to that older condition verbatim
using InstanceTypeChecker::IsJSSpecialApiObject(target->map()->instance_type()).
In Map::Normalize() the branch still spells IsUndefined(x, isolate); kept.

